    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s542-when-we-use-it",
      "source": "sections/s542-when-we-use-it.md",
      "source_hash": "bb4f52cf0beb8d78bdfc7952d45aedf750e4b0bd35f6a474fe3bf56386d85259",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The retry-tracker script is used when requests to external systems have failed because of network or service problems and need to be sent again.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s543-how-it-works",
      "source": "sections/s543-how-it-works.md",
      "source_hash": "a50a00cf30571e55848ee3dafc453235f6aeab973c839e40c13b2e233d9f9565",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "How the retry-tracker script works. It finds the URLs marked as failed in the OpenURLTracker table and sends those requests again, which helps after temporary network or service failures. The -a option adds a test URL to the table so the script can be tried without waiting for a real failure.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s544-parameters",
      "source": "sections/s544-parameters.md",
      "source_hash": "9fd23308647acf8fd550b2cc1078ebf0e4eb1a2899a93b926b25f51629e3b28f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Parameters of the retry-tracker script: -a <value> adds a \"failed\" row with a URL, for testing only; -r retries every URL in the table of failed requests, including one added with -a; -h/--help prints help.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s545-conclusion-quickguide",
      "source": "sections/s545-conclusion-quickguide.md",
      "source_hash": "624e6a92cb1850f71f8b085ef333bd2c53acb2eff2738a40e247bbfca6229b49",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Closing quick guide for the retry-tracker script: it resends failed requests to external systems so they are not lost to temporary network or service problems, and is worth adding to the workflow when such failures are frequent.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
