    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s549-when-we-use-it",
      "source": "sections/s549-when-we-use-it.md",
      "source_hash": "79061bfbd0e889a5443c149cd2284732add3c2c343f4fa08e603d59b847865ee",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The solr-database-resync script is used when the database and the Solr index disagree, for example after the database was changed outside DSpace or indexing failed, so that item statuses in Solr no longer match and search results are wrong.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s550-how-it-works",
      "source": "sections/s550-how-it-works.md",
      "source_hash": "5b2c2eab322ab6b4c69dd94f2d74abaaeba9f41eef8ce613cc43af96e8305418",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "How the solr-database-resync script works. Each item's metadata is stored in the database and indexed in Solr, where a status field says whether the item is in archive, withdrawn or discoverable. The script reads all items and their status from the Solr index, checks each against the database, updates the database status where needed, and then reindexes each item so Solr holds the correct status.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s551-parameters",
      "source": "sections/s551-parameters.md",
      "source_hash": "8d72515e86e74b72e94794e22eb96e7434fd3ffb99b9a1830dc9189a49f77e39",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The solr-database-resync script takes no parameters.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s552-conclusion-quickguide",
      "source": "sections/s552-conclusion-quickguide.md",
      "source_hash": "04951b2c49eb7b09fd004c3b41d84f1ecf41b07201b88ba9edd93b2617fda9ca",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Closing quick guide for the solr-database-resync script. It brings the database and the Solr index back in line, but it can change the status of many items, so use it only when needed and back up the database first. It can help diagnose and fix wrong search results or item statuses.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
